msgstr "Responsable"

#: apps/users/models.py:241
msgid "Administrator"
msgstr "Administración"

#: apps/users/models.py:289
msgid "Null only for platform superusers on self-hosted installs."
msgstr ""
"Vacío solo para superusuarios de plataforma en instalaciones autoalojadas."

#: apps/users/models.py:313
msgid "email address"
msgstr "correo electrónico"

#: apps/users/models.py:315
msgid "first name"
msgstr "nombre"

#: apps/users/models.py:318
msgid "last name"
msgstr "apellidos"

#: apps/users/models.py:320
msgid "role"
msgstr "perfil"

#: apps/users/models.py:322
msgid "staff number"
msgstr "nº de empleado"

#: apps/users/models.py:326
msgid ""
"The person's identifier in the company's own systems. Acts as a bridge when "
"an external application records clock events on their behalf."
msgstr ""
"El identificador de la persona en los sistemas de la propia empresa. Sirve "
"de puente cuando una aplicación externa registra fichajes en su nombre."

#: apps/users/models.py:334
msgid "Overrides the company language for this person."
msgstr "Sustituye el idioma de la empresa para esta persona."

#: apps/users/models.py:346
msgid "working-time regime"
msgstr "régimen de jornada"

#: apps/users/models.py:350
msgid "Art. 3.b. Decides which limits apply, not just how many hours."
msgstr "Art. 3.b. Decide qué límites se aplican, no solo cuántas horas."

#: apps/users/models.py:353
msgid "contracted hours"
msgstr "horas contratadas"

#: apps/users/models.py:359
msgid ""
"The figure the contract agreed. Empty on a full-time contract means the "
"company's own; empty with no agreed figure means there is none."
msgstr ""
"La cifra que pactó el contrato. Vacío en jornada completa significa la de la "
"empresa; vacío sin cifra pactada significa que no la hay."

#: apps/users/models.py:364
msgid "over"
msgstr "sobre"

#: apps/users/models.py:368
msgid "Whether the figure above is a week, a month or a year."
msgstr "Si la cifra anterior es semanal, mensual o anual."

#: apps/users/models.py:377
msgid "contract starts"
msgstr "el contrato empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:380
msgid "Empty means it was already running when the company started here."
msgstr ""
"Vacío significa que ya estaba en marcha cuando la empresa empezó a usar esto."

#: apps/users/models.py:383
msgid "contract ends"
msgstr "el contrato acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:386
msgid "Empty means open-ended. A date makes it fixed-term."
msgstr "Vacío significa indefinido. Con fecha, es temporal."

#: apps/users/models.py:405
msgid "relieves"
msgstr "releva a"

#: apps/users/models.py:406
msgid "Art. 12.7: who this relief contract stands in for."
msgstr "Art. 12.7: a quién sustituye este contrato de relevo."

#: apps/users/models.py:410
msgid "permanent seasonal"
msgstr "fijo discontinuo"

#: apps/users/models.py:413
msgid ""
"Art. 16 ET: the work comes in periods of activity. Outside them there is no "
"expected working day, and the roster says so instead of reporting an absence."
msgstr ""
"Art. 16 ET: el trabajo viene por periodos de actividad. Fuera de ellos no "
"hay jornada prevista, y el cuadrante lo dice en vez de contarlo como una "
"ausencia."

#: apps/users/models.py:419
msgid "agreed hours"
msgstr "horario pactado"

#: apps/users/models.py:423
msgid ""
"Art. 3.b: the agreed working hours, as text. For example 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Free text because a schedule is not a shape a closed field can hold."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.b: el horario pactado, como texto. Por ejemplo 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Texto libre porque un horario no tiene una forma que quepa en un campo "
"cerrado."

#: apps/users/models.py:433
msgid "night worker"
msgstr "trabajador nocturno"

#: apps/users/models.py:438
msgid ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. A status, not a shift: three hours of the daily working day at "
"night as a rule, or a third of the year. It brings an eight-hour average "
"over fifteen days and a ban on overtime. Leave it on automatic to read it "
"from the roster."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. Es una condición de la persona, no del turno: normalmente tres "
"horas de la jornada diaria en horario nocturno, o un tercio de la jornada "
"anual. Trae un promedio de ocho horas en quince días y la prohibición de "
"horas extraordinarias. Déjalo en automático para leerlo del cuadrante."

#: apps/users/models.py:445
msgid "rotating shifts"
msgstr "turnos rotativos"

#: apps/users/models.py:448
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. The person rotates between shift teams. This does not add "
"limits: it stops the ordinary ones being applied to a changeover, where a "
"shorter rest is lawful and owed back rather than a breach."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. La persona rota entre equipos de turno. Esto no añade límites: "
"evita que se apliquen los ordinarios a un relevo, donde un descanso más "
"corto es lícito y se devuelve, no se incumple."

#: apps/users/models.py:454
msgid "volunteered for nights"
msgstr "adscripción voluntaria a noches"

#: apps/users/models.py:457
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET allows more than two consecutive weeks on the night shift only "
"when the person asked for it. Recorded here because the roster cannot tell a "
"volunteer from somebody left there."
msgstr ""
"El art. 36.3 ET permite más de dos semanas consecutivas en el turno de noche "
"solo si la persona lo ha pedido. Se anota aquí porque el cuadrante no "
"distingue a quien se ofrece de a quien dejan ahí."

#: apps/users/models.py:464
msgid "usual mode"
msgstr "modalidad habitual"

#: apps/users/models.py:469
msgid ""
"Art. 3.e. What a clock event assumes when it says nothing; each event can "
"still record the other."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.e. Lo que asume un fichaje cuando no dice nada; cada uno puede "
"registrar la otra modalidad."

#: apps/users/models.py:475
msgid "date of birth"
msgstr "fecha de nacimiento"

#: apps/users/models.py:479
msgid ""
"Only used to apply the protections the law gives workers under eighteen: "
"eight hours a day, a thirty-minute break from four and a half, two days of "
"weekly rest, and no night work or overtime. Without it those protections "
"cannot be applied, and the system says so rather than assuming the person is "
"an adult."
msgstr ""
"Solo se usa para aplicar las protecciones que la ley da a los menores de "
"dieciocho años: ocho horas diarias, treinta minutos de descanso a partir de "
"cuatro y media, dos días de descanso semanal, y ni trabajo nocturno ni horas "
"extraordinarias. Sin ella no se pueden aplicar, y el sistema lo dice en vez "
"de dar por hecho que la persona es mayor de edad."

#: apps/users/models.py:491
msgid "workers' representative"
msgstr "representante de las personas trabajadoras"

#: apps/users/models.py:494
msgid ""
"Informed when somebody disagrees with a change to their record (art. 4.b), "
"and entitled to consult the register (art. 6.2)."
msgstr ""
"Se le informa cuando alguien discrepa de un cambio en su registro (art. "
"4.b), y tiene derecho a consultar el registro (art. 6.2)."

#: apps/users/models.py:504
msgid "wants clock reminders"
msgstr "quiere recordatorios de fichaje"

#: apps/users/models.py:507
msgid ""
"Send a reminder when a shift starts and there is no entry, or when a day is "
"left open. It prompts the real punch; it never records one."
msgstr ""
"Envía un recordatorio si empieza el turno y no hay entrada, o si queda una "
"jornada abierta. Empuja al fichaje real, nunca registra uno."

#: apps/users/models.py:517
msgid ""
"Overrides the company figure for this person. Empty means the company's. "
"Part-time and mid-year joiners are the usual reason."
msgstr ""
"Sustituye la cifra de la empresa para esta persona. Vacío significa la de la "
"empresa. Lo habitual es la jornada parcial y las altas a mitad de periodo."

#: apps/users/models.py:529
msgid "identity provider subject"
msgstr "identificador en el proveedor de identidad"

#: apps/users/models.py:534
msgid "issuer"
msgstr "emisor"

#: apps/users/models.py:537
msgid "admin site access"
msgstr "acceso al sitio de administración"

#: apps/users/models.py:538
msgid "date joined"
msgstr "fecha de alta"

#: apps/users/models.py:546
msgid "person"
msgstr "persona"

#: apps/users/models.py:547
msgid "people"
msgstr "personas"

#: apps/users/models.py:819
msgid "activity starts"
msgstr "la actividad empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:821
msgid "activity ends"
msgstr "la actividad acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:824
msgid "Empty while the season is open: a campaign knows when it starts."
msgstr ""
"Vacío mientras la temporada siga abierta: una campaña sabe cuándo empieza."

#: apps/users/models.py:827
msgid "called up on"
msgstr "llamamiento el"

#: apps/users/models.py:831
msgid ""
"Art. 16.3 ET: the call-up is in writing and with notice. The date is what "
"shows the notice was given; a tick would not."
msgstr ""
"Art. 16.3 ET: el llamamiento es por escrito y con antelación. La fecha es lo "
"que demuestra que se avisó; una casilla marcada, no."

#: apps/users/models.py:838
msgid "period of activity"
msgstr "periodo de actividad"

#: apps/users/models.py:839
msgid "periods of activity"
msgstr "periodos de actividad"

#: apps/users/models.py:892
msgid "signed on"
msgstr "firmado el"

#: apps/users/models.py:893
msgid "Art. 5.1: the agreement comes before the remote work starts."
msgstr "Art. 5.1: el acuerdo va antes de que empiece el trabajo a distancia."

#: apps/users/models.py:895
msgid "remote work starts"
msgstr "el trabajo a distancia empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:897
msgid "remote work ends"
msgstr "el trabajo a distancia acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:900
msgid "Empty for an open-ended agreement, which is the usual one."
msgstr "Vacío para un acuerdo sin fecha de fin, que es el corriente."

#: apps/users/models.py:903
msgid "share agreed (%)"
msgstr "porcentaje pactado (%)"

#: apps/users/models.py:909
msgid ""
"Art. 7.f asks the agreement to state it. Left empty it is not checked "
"against what is actually worked: the figure that binds is on paper."
msgstr ""
"El art. 7.f pide que el acuerdo lo diga. Vacío no se contrasta con lo que se "
"trabaja de verdad: la cifra que obliga es la del papel."

#: apps/users/models.py:916
msgid "remote work agreement"
msgstr "acuerdo de trabajo a distancia"

#: apps/users/models.py:917
msgid "remote work agreements"
msgstr "acuerdos de trabajo a distancia"

#: apps/users/models.py:953
msgid "In negotiation"
msgstr "En negociación"

#: apps/users/models.py:954
msgid "Accepted"
msgstr "Aceptada"

#: apps/users/models.py:955
msgid "An alternative was proposed"
msgstr "Se propuso una alternativa"

#: apps/users/models.py:956
msgid "Refused"
msgstr "Denegada"

#: apps/users/models.py:957
msgid "Withdrawn by the person"
msgstr "Retirada por la persona"

#: apps/users/models.py:995
msgid "requested on"
msgstr "solicitada el"

#: apps/users/models.py:996
msgid "The fifteen days of art. 34.8 count from here."
msgstr "Los quince días del art. 34.8 se cuentan desde aquí."

#: apps/users/models.py:999
msgid "what is being asked"
msgstr "qué se pide"

#: apps/users/models.py:1001
msgid ""
"Duration, distribution, or the way the work is done --- remote included."
msgstr ""
"Duración, distribución o forma de prestación ---incluido a distancia---."

#: apps/users/models.py:1009
msgid "answered on"
msgstr "contestada el"

#: apps/users/models.py:1011
msgid "answer"
msgstr "respuesta"

#: apps/users/models.py:1015
msgid ""
"Art. 34.8 asks for this in writing, and for a reason when the answer is not "
"a plain yes."
msgstr ""
"El art. 34.8 lo pide por escrito, y con motivo cuando la respuesta no es un "
"sí a secas."

#: apps/users/models.py:1025
msgid "answered by"
msgstr "contestada por"

#: apps/users/models.py:1029
msgid "schedule adaptation"
msgstr "adaptación de jornada"

#: apps/users/models.py:1030
msgid "schedule adaptations"
msgstr "adaptaciones de jornada"

#: apps/users/passwords.py:138
#, python-format
msgid "Your account at %(company)s"
msgstr "Tu cuenta en %(company)s"

#: apps/users/passwords.py:140
#, python-format
msgid "Reset your password at %(company)s"
msgstr "Restablecer tu contraseña en %(company)s"

#: apps/users/serializers.py:87
#, python-format
msgid "%(code)s is not a region of %(country)s."
msgstr "%(code)s no es una comunidad de %(country)s."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:223
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(name)s does not have a manager profile, so putting them in charge would "
"grant nothing."
msgstr ""
"%(name)s no tiene perfil de responsable, así que ponerle al frente no le "
"daría nada."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:350
msgid "Somebody in this company already uses it."
msgstr "Ya lo usa alguien de esta empresa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:382
#, python-format
msgid "%(name)s already uses that staff number."
msgstr "%(name)s ya usa ese número de empleado."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:398
msgid "That department belongs to another company."
msgstr "Ese departamento es de otra empresa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:414
msgid "It cannot be today or a future date."
msgstr "No puede ser hoy ni una fecha futura."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:423
#, python-format
msgid "That gives an age of %(age)s, below the minimum working age. %(basis)s"
msgstr ""
"Eso da una edad de %(age)s años, por debajo de la edad mínima para trabajar. "
"%(basis)s"

#: apps/users/serializers.py:427
msgid "That gives an age of over a hundred years."
msgstr "Eso da una edad de más de cien años."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:452
msgid ""
"There is no agreed figure on this regime. Clear it, or choose one that has "
"hours."
msgstr ""
"En este régimen no hay cifra pactada. Bórrala, o elige uno que tenga horas."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:469
msgid "Art. 3.b asks for the agreed hours on this regime."
msgstr "El art. 3.b pide las horas pactadas en este régimen."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:484
msgid "A relief contract stands in for somebody else."
msgstr "Un contrato de relevo sustituye a otra persona."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:493
msgid "It has to be above zero."
msgstr "Tiene que ser mayor que cero."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:513
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(basis)s: workers under eighteen may not work at night, so the status "
"cannot apply to them."
msgstr ""
"%(basis)s: los menores de dieciocho años no pueden trabajar de noche, así "
"que esa condición no les puede corresponder."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:532
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(hours)s h a week is above the company's %(ceiling)s h. A contract cannot "
"agree past the legal maximum."
msgstr ""
"%(hours)s h semanales pasan de las %(ceiling)s h de la empresa. Un contrato "
"no puede pactar por encima del máximo legal."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:581
msgid "A company with this tax number already exists."
msgstr "Ya existe una empresa con este identificador fiscal."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:645 apps/users/serializers.py:658
msgid "Wrong credentials."
msgstr "Credenciales incorrectas."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:759
msgid ""
"Art. 34.8 asks for a reason when the answer is an alternative or a refusal."
msgstr ""
"El art. 34.8 pide un motivo cuando la respuesta es una alternativa o una "
"negativa."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:774
msgid "An answer needs the date it was given."
msgstr "Una respuesta necesita la fecha en que se dio."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:818
msgid "A share goes from 0 to 100."
msgstr "Un porcentaje va de 0 a 100."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:838
msgid "The agreement cannot end before it starts."
msgstr "El acuerdo no puede acabar antes de empezar."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:856
#, python-format
msgid "It overlaps the agreement that starts on %(day)s."
msgstr "Se solapa con el acuerdo que empieza el %(day)s."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:897
msgid "Periods of activity are for permanent-seasonal contracts (art. 16 ET)."
msgstr ""
"Los periodos de actividad son para contratos fijos discontinuos (art. 16 ET)."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:916
msgid "The season cannot end before it starts."
msgstr "La temporada no puede acabar antes de empezar."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:923
msgid "The call-up comes before the season starts, not after."
msgstr "El llamamiento va antes de que empiece la temporada, no después."

#: apps/users/serializers.py:936
#, python-format
msgid "It overlaps the period that starts on %(day)s."
msgstr "Se solapa con el periodo que empieza el %(day)s."

#: apps/users/views.py:214
msgid "No session to renew."
msgstr "No hay sesión que renovar."

#: apps/users/views.py:243
msgid "The session has expired. Sign in again."
msgstr "La sesión ha caducado. Vuelve a entrar."

#: apps/users/views.py:266
msgid "Send the refresh token to close the session."
msgstr "Manda el testigo de refresco para cerrar la sesión."

#: apps/users/views.py:459
msgid ""
"This is the only active administrator. Appoint another one first, or the "
"company is left with nobody able to manage it."
msgstr ""
"Es el único administrador activo. Nombra antes a otro, o la empresa se queda "
"sin nadie que pueda gestionarla."

#: apps/users/views.py:514
msgid "This account signs in through your identity provider."
msgstr "Esta cuenta entra a través de vuestro proveedor de identidad."

#: apps/users/views.py:516
msgid "Reactivate the account before inviting them."
msgstr "Vuelve a dar de alta la cuenta antes de invitarla."

#: apps/users/views.py:542
msgid "There is no address to send it to. Add one first."
msgstr "No hay ninguna dirección a la que mandarlo. Añade una antes."

#: apps/users/views.py:617
msgid "You cannot erase your own account."
msgstr "No puedes borrar tu propia cuenta."

#: apps/users/views.py:629
#, python-format
msgid "what is theirs: %(cosas)s"
msgstr "lo suyo: %(cosas)s"

#: apps/users/views.py:632
#, python-format
msgid "what they decided about other people: %(cosas)s"
msgstr "lo que decidió sobre otras personas: %(cosas)s"

#: apps/users/views.py:638
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(quien)s left a record, so their file has to stay and explain it --- "
"%(que)s. Deactivate them instead."
msgstr ""
"%(quien)s dejó rastro, así que su ficha tiene que quedarse y explicarlo --- "
"%(que)s. Dale de baja en su lugar."

#: apps/users/views.py:680
msgid "You cannot deactivate your own account."
msgstr "No puedes dar de baja tu propia cuenta."

#: apps/users/views.py:736
#, python-format
msgid "Left on %(day)s. %(count)s shift(s) still rostered after that."
msgstr "Se fue el %(day)s. Le quedan %(count)s turno(s) planificados después."

#: apps/users/views.py:739
#, python-format
msgid "Left on %(day)s."
msgstr "Se fue el %(day)s."

#: apps/users/views.py:795
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(count)s people answer for this department. Move them first: leaving them "
"in charge of nothing means they can no longer read anybody's record but "
"their own."
msgstr ""
"De este departamento responden %(count)s personas. Muévelas primero: al "
"mando de nada, dejan de poder leer los datos de nadie más que los suyos."

#: apps/users/views.py:843
#, python-format
msgid ""
"%(count)s people work there. Move them first: without a workplace they lose "
"their local holidays and their time zone."
msgstr ""
"Ahí trabajan %(count)s personas. Muévelas primero: sin centro pierden sus "
"festivos locales y su zona horaria."

#: apps/users/views.py:898
msgid "The link is not valid or has already been used."
msgstr "El enlace no es válido o ya se ha usado."

#: apps/users/views.py:978
msgid "A schedule adaptation can only be asked for by the person themselves."
msgstr "Una adaptación de jornada solo la puede pedir la propia persona."

#: apps/users/views.py:998
msgid "Only an administrator answers a schedule adaptation."
msgstr "Solo administración contesta una adaptación de jornada."

